Given the head of a singly linked list, reverse the list, and return the reversed list.

Example 1:
1->2->3->4->5---null
5->4->3->2->1---null

there will be 
pre = null for 1->null
and next = curr.next
curr = 1
next = 2

we are fliping
1->2  t0 null<-1->2

now you have flipped
current.next to pre
now update as we move to next node
pre will be current - prev = curr
curr will be the next coming node - curr = next

class Solution {
    public ListNode reverseList(ListNode head) {
        if(head == null) return head;//1,2,3,4,5
        ListNode current = head;
        ListNode prev = null; //previous to reverse -> last one will be null
        while(current!=null){ 
        ListNode next = current.next; //2//3//4//5//null
        current.next = prev; //1->null//2->1//3->2//4->3//5->4
        prev = current; //1//2//3//4//5
        current = next; //2//3//4//5//null
        }
        return prev;
    }
}
